infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Mock vs fake: testing the double, or testing behavior
  desc A mock asserts interactions and encodes the implementation; a fake asserts state and survives refactors
  compares
    - label Mock — asserts interactions
      children
        - label Pins method, args, order, count
          desc Encodes the current call sequence of the code
        - label Shatters on equivalent refactors
          desc Reorder two independent reads, 214 tests red
        - label Too obedient to catch real bugs
          desc Returns what the author assumed, not the gateway
        - label Right only when the call IS the behavior
          desc Audit log written exactly once on failure
    - label Fake — asserts state
      children
        - label Small working impl, map behind a mutex
          desc About 20 lines, written once, reused across tests
        - label Survives any behavior-preserving refactor
          desc Answers honestly whoever calls in any order
        - label Honors the real contract
          desc Not-found returns ErrNotFound; Save then Get round-trips
        - label Failure injection is one field
          desc Add failNextSave error, set it in the test
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
